# Line endings.
#
# Every source file in this repository is written with LF. Git on Windows
# defaults to converting them to CRLF on checkout, which is where the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings come from — dozens of them, on every
# `git add`, saying nothing useful.
#
# This settles it: the repository stores LF, and checkouts get LF on every
# platform. Windows editors have handled LF for years, and the alternative is
# a repository whose line endings depend on which machine last touched it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep these byte-for-byte whatever the setting above says.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
*.aab binary
*.apk binary
